From aec82b16affd02baf7a33af802c5ec21bb30d953 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:37:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] AP Isolation: Off / Wi-Fi only / Wi-Fi and LAN ports on every
 network

- Since GPL 102.40585 the firmware isolated the main network's wired ports as well when AP Isolation was
  on, so wired devices could no longer reach each other (a TV could not find a NAS). AP Isolation is now
  a choice per network: Wi-Fi only (default: Wi-Fi devices cannot reach each other, wired devices stay
  reachable) or Wi-Fi and LAN ports (the router's LAN ports are kept apart too). Both lines behave the
  same.
- Never isolated: the WAN ports, VLAN trunk ports and a port with an AiMesh node behind it. A guest
  network's trunk to AiMesh nodes keeps the firmware's isolation with either choice. A network whose VLAN
  profile sets port isolation, a Guest Portal and the AiMesh backhaul network are left as they are. On an
  AiMesh node the firmware's own behaviour applies.
- The watchdog re-checks the ports while a network uses Wi-Fi and LAN ports. nvram is never changed.
- Network page: the choice under the AP Isolation switch; the VLAN tab clears a reused network's guest
  path and isolation settings. sdn.js also carries the previous commit's guest-path rows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
